WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.190
Your French friend texts: «On
va au cinéma ce soir ?» «On».

2
00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.020
Not «nous». So who is going?

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.360
You? Them? Everyone?

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.830
Then you write back.

5
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.080
English has one word for 'you'.

6
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.220
French has two: «tu» and «vous».

7
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.450
Your best friend.

8
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.870
Then your teacher.

9
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.410
Do you pick the same one?

10
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.330
So why does French have
two words for 'you',

11
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.240
and when does «on» mean 'we'?

12
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.770
In this mission, you'll
fill in the pronoun grid

13
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.320
and follow the flowchart
for «tu» and «vous».

14
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.340
Then you'll hear the linking
sounds that change a verb,

15
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.990
and match subjects to verbs in the lab.

16
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.880
Your mission: work out which 'you' to use,

17
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.150
and when «on» means 'we'.
